title: The Grand Synthesis — Shared Knowledge Banks, Deep Scans, and Portable Armories
summary: 'Three convergent ideas completing the agent architecture vision: (1) Shared knowledge banks with concept-level abstraction — not raw snippets but universal principles with language-specific implementations, enabling compendiums that even small local models can leverage. (2) Deep knowledge scans (paradigm scan --learn) using multi-agent fleet to extract patterns, anti-patterns, conventions, and monitors from existing codebases — solving the cold-start problem. (3) Portable agent state via git-backed ~/.paradigm/ sync across machines with selective, anonymized sharing for community contribution. Privacy non-negotiable: default private, opt-in sharing, per-entry anonymization, revocation.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-mcp'
decisions:
  - id: compendium-concept-level
    decision: Knowledge sharing should happen at concept level with language-specific implementations, not raw snippet dumps
    rationale: Concepts transfer across languages. Snippets don't. Concept graphs enable polyglot agents and community merging without naming/convention conflicts.
  - id: sync-via-git
    decision: Agent portability Phase 1 uses git-backed ~/.paradigm/ sync — no infrastructure needed
    rationale: Simplest path. Version history, offline-capable, rollback trivial. Private repo = private agents. No server dependency.
  - id: privacy-default-private
    decision: All agent/notebook data is private by default. Sharing is opt-in, per-entry, with mandatory anonymization
    rationale: Trust is non-negotiable. Proprietary codebase knowledge must never leak. Universal patterns can be extracted and shared without exposing business logic.
